{"file": "VERIFICATION_STRATEGY.md", "opening": "# clanker verification strategy\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUse the intended experience to choose what to investigate, inspect the relevant Hermes implementation, then test that behavior in a small controlled environment. Repeat for each part of the experience. Add clanker code only after identifying a concrete gap that configuration or a supported extension cannot close.\n\n[V1_SCOPE.md](production/V1_SCOPE.md) remains the product contract. This file records how to verify it; it does not expand the scope or approve an implementation. The [Hermes review](HERMES_VERIFICATION_REVIEW.md) records documentation/source findings. A [pinned local baseline](verification/LOCAL_BASELINE.md) now starts and passes 47 targeted upstream routing/session tests. [Owner-only CLI, Slack DM and channel mention inference](verification/evidence/2026-10-03-model-slack-smoke.md) also pass with tools disabled. All complete clanker runtime acceptance scenarios remain open.\n\n## Now\n"}
{"file": "POC_SCOPE.md", "opening": "# Clanker local Slack POC\n\n**Response defaults:** all existing and newly provisioned private/shared contexts use the concise personality. Users give tasks in natural language; Clanker handles tool selection and technical details. First-use command tips, profile-building offers, home-channel setup prompts and raw tool progress are disabled. Apply the existing-profile settings with `scripts/configure-clanker-style`; new profiles receive them during provisioning.\n\n**Implementation checkpoint \u2014 5 October 2026:** automatic workspace onboarding and private/shared routing are live. The real third member was provisioned before first contact and received one welcome within three seconds. Its DM and both channels passed ordinary browser tasks after enabling the verified Seatbelt-backed native tools across all five contexts. Fresh browser-ready join provisioning and failure recovery passed with native profiles and fixture Slack transport. [Join evidence](verification/evidence/2026-10-05-slack-onboarding-mod.md), [browser execution and limits](verification/evidence/2026-10-05-browser-execution.md).\n\nCurrent delivery decision: 4 October 2026. The MacBook is the POC host. Cloud hosting, Cloudflare billing, worker VM pools and laptop-independent availability are deferred for this POC.\n\n**Execution decision \u2014 5 October 2026:** use macOS `sandbox-exec` for this local POC, with one common policy template parameterized for each private or shared execution context. Record its deprecation and macOS dependency as the local fallback's known limits; VM/container execution remains a future upgrade. The actual Browser Use executor, terminal and Chromium process tree are constrained; Chromium's inner sandbox is disabled while the outer Seatbelt boundary remains required. Metadata exposure and absent quotas remain known limits. [Decision, acceptance checks and assignment note](docs/decisions/2026-10-05-local-execution-boundary.md).\n"}
{"file": "production/README.md", "opening": "# Clanker production design\n\nDeferred production design, preserved for the assignment's known-limitations and improvements discussion. The current build and delivery scope is the [local POC](../POC_SCOPE.md).\n\n## Design notes\n\n- [Design decisions](DESIGN_DECISIONS.md): selected architecture, reasons, tradeoffs, open proposals and improvements considered.\n- [Original v1 scope](V1_SCOPE.md): the detailed hosted-product scope before the POC pivot.\n- [Gateway review draft](SLACK_GATEWAY_PRD.md): task routing, private/shared contexts, isolated workers and recovery contracts. Its integration choices remain proposals.\n"}
